  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted (config_027) is the clear best at 0.7062, with scvi_n200 outperforming pca_n2000 by ~7 points and imagenet_vit_l outperforming resnet50 by ~3 points. However, we have zero information about scgpt as an RNA encoder. Question: Does scgpt, paired with the best-known image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (weighted), match or exceed scvi_n200? Why: With 4 experiments remaining after this one, testing the one unexplored RNA encoder under otherwise optimal settings is the highest-information experiment. If scgpt is competitive, it opens new combinations; if it lags significantly, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can spend remaining budget on fine-grained fusion/aggregation variants around the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l core."
}

